# Drafted by Gemini (R21 parade), edited.

~ begin
set parade_begun
if quest.twelve_costumes == asked
quest twelve_costumes lost
endif
if quest.free_the_bell == asked
quest free_the_bell silenced
endif
if quest.fools_day == revelry
if not quest.fools_day >= parade
quest fools_day parade
endif
endif
Narrator: A high brass bell tolls without a hand on the rope, and the painted ribbons snap taut overhead. All around the square, the costumed dancers stiffen and fall into a single marching line.
if flag.told_chuckles_hate
chuckles [angry]: Look at your eyes, little heroes. That hate is good, thick and dark and nourishing, just the meat to feed a proper parade.
else
chuckles [smile]: Hip-hip-hooray, hip-hip-heroes, hear the drum-drum! All your dearest chum-chums are marching right up front to lead my grand parade!
endif
Narrator: Two tall figures in spotless porcelain harlequin masks step out of the parting throng, heavy banner poles balanced across their shoulders.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Those two are billed as headliners, darling, and stitched for trouble.
chuckles [smile]: Make way, make way for the finest pair in the whole wide festy-val! Put your hands together for my glorious Heralds of Fools!
combat parade_heralds

~ unmask
cutscene fd_unmasking
Narrator: A hairline crack runs from brow to chin across both white porcelain faces, and the halves shell away onto the cobbles.
cutscene fd_unmasking_2
phillip_druskenvald [smile]: My word, Adela darling, what a perfectly splendid crush of people! I do believe the punch has spilled right down my collar, though it tastes awfully of iron.
interject name:cordelia_skein: Arterial iron under porcelain glaze. They do not even register their own pathology, darling.
adela_druskenvald [smile]: Nonsense, Phillip dearest, it is only theatrical paint, and the music is simply divine! Look how our dear friends have come to dance with us.
chuckles [sly]: Oh, bravo, tip-top and tweedle-dee, you played your parts so sweet-sweet! Now take a little bow-bow before the curtain drops.
cutscene fd_unmasking_3
Narrator: Where the jester's gloved fingertips brush their cheeks, lord and lady pop like paper lanterns into ribbons of red and gold that scatter on the night wind.
set druskenvalds_unmasked
set phillip_adela_taken
if not quest.fools_day >= ring_of_fools
quest fools_day ring_of_fools
endif
Narrator: With a single shuffling step, the masked crowd turns its back on the empty cobbles and marches toward the blazing torches of the Ring of Fools.
move fd_ring_of_fools:from_parade
